{
  "Engineering. Art. A curious mind.": "工程、藝術，以及一顆好奇的心。",
  "I'm a software and AI engineer, photographer, and world traveller. This is a collection of things I've made and things that made me look twice.": "我是一位軟體與 AI 工程師、攝影者，也是一個喜歡旅行的人。這裡收藏著我做過的東西，以及那些讓我忍不住多看一眼的事物。",
  "An engineer with an artist's eye.": "帶著藝術家眼光的工程師。",
  "I'm Dheera Venkatraman — a software and AI engineer, photographer, and world traveller based in the San Francisco Bay Area. I like understanding how things work, making things that don't exist yet, and finding a different way to look at something familiar.\n\n## Engineering and imagination\n\nMy work spans generative AI, computer vision, robotics, and imaging. I'm a Principal Engineer at Wayve, where I work on generative models for evaluating autonomous driving. Previously, I worked at Amazon and Freedom Robotics, and co-founded Robby Technologies, building autonomous delivery robots. I have a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering from MIT, where my research included single-photon imaging.\n\nThat technical background is also part of how I make art. A camera can be an instrument for seeing beyond ordinary perception: the heat of an Icelandic landscape, or the scale of a nebula above a mountain. I enjoy the space where a technical experiment becomes an image, an experience, or something useful.\n\n## Across places and cultures\n\nI've never had a simple answer to “Where are you from?” I'm a third-culture kid; language, culture, nationality, and belonging don't line up neatly for me. I feel at home moving between places and perspectives.\n\nTravel and photography give that curiosity somewhere to go. I like paying attention to light, landscapes, and the details of everyday life — and bringing some of those observations back into the things I build.\n\n## Things made out of curiosity\n\nMost of my professional engineering happens inside companies. This site is a home for the work I can share: photographs, open-source tools, physical builds, and occasional experiments on the web.\n\nIf something here sparks a conversation, [say hello](mailto:dheera@dheera.net).": "我是 Dheera Venkatraman，一位住在舊金山灣區的軟體與 AI 工程師、攝影者，也是一個喜歡旅行的人。我喜歡弄懂事物如何運作，做出還不存在的東西，並用不同的角度看待熟悉的事物。\n\n## 工程與想像力\n\n我的工作涵蓋生成式 AI、電腦視覺、機器人與成像技術。目前我在 Wayve 擔任 Principal Engineer，研究與開發用於評估自動駕駛的生成式模型。此前，我曾在 Amazon 和 Freedom Robotics 工作，並共同創辦 Robby Technologies，打造自主配送機器人。我在 MIT 取得電機工程博士學位，研究內容包括單光子成像。\n\n這些技術背景也影響著我的藝術創作。相機可以成為看見日常感知之外世界的工具：冰島地景的熱量，或山巒上方星雲的尺度。我喜歡探索技術實驗如何變成一幅影像、一種體驗，或一件有用的東西。\n\n## 在地方與文化之間\n\n對於「你是哪裡人？」這個問題，我從來沒有簡單的答案。我是一個第三文化小孩；語言、文化、國籍與歸屬感，對我而言並不整齊地重疊。在不同地方與觀點之間移動，反而讓我感到自在。\n\n旅行與攝影讓這份好奇心有了方向。我喜歡留意光線、地景和日常生活中的細節，再把其中一些觀察帶回自己做的東西裡。\n\n## 出於好奇而做的東西\n\n我的專業工程工作大多在公司內部進行。這個網站收藏的是我能分享的部分：攝影作品、開源工具、實體創作，以及偶爾在網頁上的實驗。\n\n如果這裡的某樣東西讓你想聊聊，歡迎[打個招呼](mailto:dheera@dheera.net)。"
}
